infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What the breaking-change gate fails the PR on
  desc oasdiff diffs the new spec against the previous version — these reject existing clients, these don't
  compares
    - label Breaking — fails the PR
      children
        - label Add a required request field
          desc Every client that omits it now gets a 422
        - label Remove a response field
          desc A client that read it breaks
        - label Narrow a type
          desc Previously valid values now rejected
        - label Remove an enum value
          desc Clients still sending it fail
        - label Delete an endpoint
          desc Callers get a 404
    - label Safe — backward-compatible
      children
        - label Add an optional request field
          desc Old clients that omit it still work
        - label Add a new endpoint
          desc No existing client calls it yet
        - label Add a response field
          desc Clients ignore unknown fields
        - label Widen a type / loosen a constraint
          desc Old values stay valid
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
